172	
173	## 3. Analyzer Registry (`analysis/registry.rs`)
174	
175	The `AnalyzerRegistry` is the architectural boundary for mixed-language workspaces. Callers ask the registry which analyzer owns a path instead of hardcoding `TsAnalyzer` plus ad hoc `.rs` exceptions.
176	
177	```rust
178	//! Multi-language analyzer registry.
179	//!
180	//! This is the architectural boundary for mixed-language workspaces. Callers
181	//! ask the registry which analyzer owns a file instead of hardcoding
182	//! `TsAnalyzer` plus ad hoc `.rs` exceptions.
183	
184	use std::sync::Arc;
185	
186	use camino::Utf8Path;
187	
188	use crate::error::Result;
189	use crate::types::WorkspaceOptions;
190	
191	#[cfg(feature = "lang-ts")]
192	use super::TsAnalyzer;
193	use super::{LanguageAnalyzer, LanguageId, RustAnalyzer};
194	
195	pub struct AnalyzerRegistry {
196	    analyzers: Vec<Arc<dyn LanguageAnalyzer>>,
197	    config_hash: String,
198	}
199	
200	impl AnalyzerRegistry {
201	    pub fn from_workspace_opts(opts: &WorkspaceOptions) -> Result<Self> {
202	        let mut analyzers: Vec<Arc<dyn LanguageAnalyzer>> = Vec::new();
203	        let mut hash_parts: Vec<String> = Vec::new();
204	
205	        #[cfg(feature = "lang-ts")]
206	        {
207	            analyzers.push(Arc::new(TsAnalyzer::from_workspace_opts(opts)?));
208	            hash_parts.push(TsAnalyzer::config_hash_for(opts));
209	        }
210	
211	        analyzers.push(Arc::new(RustAnalyzer::from_workspace_opts(opts)));
212	        hash_parts.push("rust-analyzer-v1".to_owned());
213	
214	        Ok(Self {
215	            analyzers,
216	            config_hash: hash_parts.join("::"),
217	        })
218	    }
219	
220	    pub fn config_hash(&self) -> &str {
221	        &self.config_hash
222	    }
223	
224	    pub fn analyzers(&self) -> &[Arc<dyn LanguageAnalyzer>] {
225	        &self.analyzers
226	    }
227	
228	    pub fn supports(&self, path: &Utf8Path) -> bool {
229	        self.analyzer_for(path).is_some()
230	    }
231	
232	    pub fn analyzer_for(&self, path: &Utf8Path) -> Option<&dyn LanguageAnalyzer> {
233	        self.analyzers
234	            .iter()
235	            .find(|analyzer| analyzer.supports(path))
236	            .map(Arc::as_ref)
237	    }
238	
239	    pub fn supports_language(&self, path: &Utf8Path, languages: &[LanguageId]) -> bool {
240	        self.analyzer_for(path)
241	            .is_some_and(|analyzer| languages.contains(&analyzer.language_id()))
242	    }
243	}
244	```
245	
246	Key properties:
247	
248	- Analyzers register in order; the first matching `supports(path)` wins. TS is registered first when `lang-ts` is enabled, Rust always.
249	- Configuration hash is composed from `TsAnalyzer::config_hash_for(opts)` plus the literal `"rust-analyzer-v1"`, joined with `::`. The composite hash flows into `crate::analysis::persist::init` for cache invalidation.
250	- `supports_language` lets language-filtered scans (e.g. `search --language rust`) check both "the analyzer recognizes this file" and "it's one of the requested languages".
251	- `Arc<dyn LanguageAnalyzer>` so the registry is shareable across rayon worker threads.
252	
