175	## 2b. `TsAnalyzer`'s completed trait impl
176	
177	Before the registry below can hold `Arc<dyn LanguageAnalyzer>`, `TsAnalyzer` needs the
178	`language_id`/`capabilities` methods §11's trait now declares. `analyze` (§17) becomes
179	`analyze_with_profile`, rebuilt on top of §2a's shared helper — v0.1.0's cache logic is
180	unchanged, TS just always answers `Some`/`true` since it does a full parse regardless of profile:
181	
182	```rust
183	impl LanguageAnalyzer for TsAnalyzer {
184	    fn language_id(&self) -> LanguageId {
185	        LanguageId::TypeScript
186	    }
187	
188	    fn supports(&self, path: &Utf8Path) -> bool {
189	        if path.as_str().ends_with(".d.ts") { return false; }
190	        matches!(path.extension(), Some("ts" | "tsx" | "js" | "jsx" | "mts" | "cts" | "mjs" | "cjs"))
191	    }
192	
193	    fn capabilities(&self) -> AnalyzerCapabilities {
194	        AnalyzerCapabilities {
195	            blocks: true,
196	            classified_imports: true,
197	            resolved_import_graph: CapabilityPrecision::Exact,
198	            refs: CapabilityPrecision::Structural,
199	            definition: CapabilityPrecision::Structural,
200	            inspect_detail: CapabilityPrecision::Structural,
201	        }
202	    }
203	
204	    fn analyze_with_profile(
205	        &self,
206	        path: &Utf8Path,
207	        source: Box<dyn FnOnce() -> Result<String>>,
208	        profile: AnalysisProfile,
209	    ) -> Result<Arc<FileAnalysis>> {
210	        cache_tiers::lookup_or_parse(
211	            path,
212	            source,
213	            profile,
214	            |persisted, _profile| Some(analysis_from_persisted(path, persisted)),
215	            |_cached, _profile| true,
216	            |src, hash, mtime_ns, size_bytes, _profile| {
217	                parse_full(self, path, src, hash, mtime_ns, size_bytes)
218	            },
219	        )
220	    }
221	}
222	```
223	
224	TS/JS always does a full parse regardless of `profile`, since `parse_full` produces
225	symbols/dependencies/exports/blocks in one OXC pass at no extra marginal cost — unlike Rust's
226	AST-vs-regex-fallback split, where a `Dependencies`-only request genuinely skips work, TS has no
227	cheaper partial path to offer, so `from_persisted`/`cached_is_valid` always answer "yes."
228	`resolved_import_graph: CapabilityPrecision::Exact` reflects `oxc_resolver`'s real module
229	resolution, not a heuristic — the only analyzer in this spec entitled to `Exact` on that field.
